A probe is a directory with three files:

* `probe.rs` — the subject side: one `#[inline(never)] pub fn` per measured
  function, written against the crates under the names `codec` and
  `storage` (and `commonware_cryptography`, `bytes`), returning plain values.
  The same text is compiled into every subject.
* `rows.rs` — the harness side: `fn cases() -> Vec<Box<dyn Case>>`, one
  `row!(set, fn, inputs, |pattern| (args..))` per entry (inputs: edge cases
  first, then generated ones, each within the function's documented
  preconditions). The helpers are in `src/main.rs`.
* `crates` — the crates the probe uses, of `codec` and `storage`: each gets a
  copy per subject (the others are not copied).

`commonware` measures the whole verified surface (varint, MMR, verifier);
`mmr-smoke` one MMR function.
